# Service layering

## Boundaries

| Package | May call |
|---------|----------|
| `offramp-api` | `fx-rate`, `ln-gateway`, `momo-gateway`, DB |
| `ln-gateway` | LND only |
| `momo-gateway` | MoMo HTTP only |
| `fx-rate` | FX sources only |

- Orchestration lives in `offramp-api` (or a dedicated worker), not inside gateways.
- Gateways expose small ports: `addHoldInvoice`, `settle`, `cancel`, `transfer`, `getStatus`.

## Handlers

```ts
// ✅ thin HTTP → validate → service → map response
export async function postQuote(req, reply) {
  const input = QuoteSchema.parse(req.body);
  const result = await offrampService.createQuote(input);
  return reply.code(201).send(toQuoteResponse(result));
}
```

- No business rules in route files.
- No raw gRPC/MoMo types leaking into HTTP JSON: map to public DTOs.

## Idempotency & state

- Every mutation keyed by `offramp_id` or deterministic MoMo `X-Reference-Id`.
- State transitions: conditional update (`WHERE status = :from`). Fail loud on conflict.
- Retries reuse the same idempotency key: never mint a second payout reference.

## Efficiency on the accept path

- On `LN_ACCEPTED`: enqueue disburse immediately; do not block the gRPC subscription handler on MoMo round-trips beyond a short handoff.
- Prefer one subscription stream per process over per-request polling.
